hadiths[64]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1322","""When the Prophet (ﷺ) arrived in Al-Madinah, they were paying in advance for fruits. So he said: 'Whoever pays in advance, then let him pay in advance for known measurements (of dates), and known weights for a specified period of time.'""


He said: There are narrations on this topic from Ibn Abi Awfa and 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abza.


 The Hadith of Ibn 'Abbas is a Hasan Sahih Hadith. This is acted upon according to the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) and others. They allow for advanced payments on food, garments and other things in which the limits and description are known. They differed over delay in delivery of animals. Some of the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) and others thought that delay in delivery of animals is allowed. This is the view of Ash-Shafi'i, Ahmad and Ishaq. Some of the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) and others, disliked delay in delivery of animals. This is the saying of Sufyan and the people of Al-Kufah. And Abu Al-Minhal's (a narrator) name is 'Abdur-Rahman bin Mut'im."
"1323","That Allah's Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever has a partner in an orchard, then he is not to sell his share of that until he proposes that to his partner.""


 The chain of this Hadith is not connected. I heard Muhammad bin Isma'il saying: It is said that ""Sulaiman Al-Yashkuri died during the lifetime of Jabir bin 'Abdullah."" He said: ""And Qatadah did not hear from him, nor did Abu Bishr."" Muhammad said: ""We do not know of any of them hearing from Sulaiman Al-Yashkuri except that 'Amr bin Dinar possibly heard from his during the lifetome of Jabir bin 'Abdullah."" He said: ""Qatadah only narrated from a writing of Sulaiman Al-Yashkuri, and he has a book from Jabir bin 'Abdullah.""


Abu Bakr Al-'Attar 'Abdul Quddus narrates to us, he said: "" 'Ali bin Al-Madini said: 'Yahya bin Sa'eed said: ""Sulaiman At-Taymi said: 'They went with the book of Jabir bin 'Abdullah to Al-Hasan Al-Basri and he took it' - or he said - 'and they reported it. Then they took it to Qatadah and reported it, so they gave it to me but I did not report it  This was narrated to us by Abu Bakr Al-'Attar from 'Ali bin Al-Madini."
"1324","# Hadith Translation

**Jābir (may Allāh be pleased with him) reported that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) prohibited *muḥāqalah*, *muzābanah*, *mukhābarah*, and *muʿāwamah*, and he granted a concession (rukhṣah) regarding *ʿarāyā*. Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.**

---

## Scholarly Notes on the Prohibited Transactions

The hadith, narrated by Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu) and recorded by al-Tirmidhī, addresses several forms of agricultural and produce-related transactions that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) prohibited due to their inherent *gharar* (excessive uncertainty) and resemblance to *ribā* (usury). The prohibited terms are as follows:

1. **Al-Muḥāqalah (المحاقلة):** Selling the wheat crop while still in the ears (i.e., grain still unthreshed) in exchange for threshed grain. This involves an uncertain measure, as the final yield is unknown.

2. **Al-Muzābanah (المزابنة):** Selling unripe dates on the palm tree in exchange for dried (tamr) dates by estimation, without actual weighing or measuring after harvest.

3. **Al-Mukhābarah (المخابرة):** A share-cropping arrangement where a landowner gives a plot to a cultivator in exchange for a portion of the yield, often involving ambiguity in the division.

4. **Al-Muʿāwamah (المعاومة):** Selling fruit crops one or two years in advance before they materialize, a form of forward contract with excessive *gharar*.

## The Concession of al-ʿArāyā (العرايا)

The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) granted a **rukhṣah** (concession) regarding *ʿarāyā*, which refers to the exchange of fresh dates on the tree for dried dates by estimation, specifically for a limited quantity (usually five *awsq* or less), to assist those in need. This exception is based on the hadith of Abū Hurayrah and others, where the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) allowed this transaction out of mercy and necessity, provided it is conducted fairly.

## Classification

Abū ʿĪsā Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī (raḥimahullāh) classified this narration as **ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ** (good and authentic), affirming its reliability in Islamic jurisprudence."
"1325","for indeed the owner of the the right has the right to speak.' Then he said: 'Purchase a camel for him and give it to him.' So they searched out but they did not find a camel but of a better ager than his camel. So he said: 'Buy it and give it to him. For indeed the best of you is the best in repaying.'"
"1326","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him):**

The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a heap of food. He inserted his hand into it, and his fingers touched moisture. He said, **""O owner of this food, what is this?""** The man said, ""It was rained upon, O Messenger of Allah."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, **""Why did you not place it on top of the food so that people could see it?""** Then he said, **""Whoever deceives is not one of us.""**

**Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** In this chapter (there are also narrations) from Ibn Umar, Abu al-Hamra', Ibn Abbas, Burayda, Abu Burda ibn Niyar, and Hudhayfa ibn al-Yaman.

**Abu Isa said:** The Hadith of Abu Hurayrah is a *hasan sahih* (good and authentic) hadith. The practice upon this is held by the people of knowledge; they regarded deception (*al-ghishsh*) as reprehensible (*makruh*) and stated that deception is *haram* (forbidden).

---

**Key Notes:**

- **"
"1327","""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took a camel of a particular age on loan. He gave back to him a camel of a better age than the one he was given. He said: 'The best among you is the best in repaying.'""


He said: There is something on this topic from Abu Rafi'.


 The Hadith of Abu Hurairah is a Hasan Sahih Hadith. Shu'bah and Sufyan reported it from Salamah.


This is acted upon according to some of the people of knowledge, they saw no harm is taking a camel of a particular age as a loan. This is the view of Ash-Shafi'i, Ahmad, and Ishaq. But some of them disliked that."
"1328","""A man behaved in a rude manner while trying to collect a debt from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). So his Companions were about to harm him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Leave him, for indeed the owner of the the right has the right to speak.' Then he said: 'Purchase a camel for him and give it to him.' So they searched out but they did not find a camel but of a better ager than his camel. So he said: 'Buy it and give it to him. For indeed the best of you is the best in repaying.'"""
"1329","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When you see someone selling or buying in the Masjid then say: 'May Allah not profit your business.' And when you see someone announcing about something lost then say: 'May Allah not return it to you.'"" The Hadith of Abu Hurairah is Hasan Gharib. This is acted upon according to some of the people of knowledge. They dislike selling and buying in the Masjid. This is the view of Ahmad and Ishaq. Some of the people of knowledge permitted selling and buying in the Masjid"
"1330","""The Messenger of Allah got a camel in advance. Some camels from the charity."" Abu Rafi' said: ""So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) told me to pay the man back for his camel. I said: 'I did not find among the camels but a superior selection of Raba'. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Give it to him, for indeed the base of people is the best of them in repaying.'""


 This Hadith is Hasan Sahih."
"1331","That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah loves tolerance in selling, tolerance in buying, and tolerance in repaying.""


He said: There is something on this topic from Jabir.


 This Hadith is Gharib. Some of them reported this Hadith from Yunus, from Sa'eed Al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah."
"1332","That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Allah forgave a man who was before you: He was tolerant when selling, tolerant when purchasing, and tolerant when repaying.""


He said: This Hadith is Gharib Sahih Hasan from this route."
"1333","That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When you see someone selling or buying in the Masjid then say: 'May Allah not profit your business.' And when you see someone announcing about something lost then say: 'May Allah not return it to you.'""


The Hadith of Abu Hurairah is Hasan Gharib. This is acted upon according to some of the people of knowledge. They dislike selling and buying in the Masjid. This is the view of Ahmad and Ishaq. Some of the people of knowledge permitted selling and buying in the Masjid."
"1334","""Go and judge between the people."" So he said: ""Perhaps you can excuse me (from that) O Commander of the Believers!"" He said: ""Why do you have an aversion for that when your father judged?"" He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: 'Whoever was a judge and judged with justice, it still would have been better for him to have turned away from it completely.' What do I want after that?'"" (Daif)."
"1335","""The judges are three: Two judges that are in the Fire, and a judge that is in Paradise. A man who judges without the truth, and he knows that. This one is in the Fire. One who judges while not knowing, ruining the rights of the people. So he is in the Fire. A judge who judges with the truth, that is the one in Paradise.""] (Daif)"
"1336","""Whoever asks for a position as a judge, then he left on his own. And whoever is forced onto it, Allah sends an angel down to him so that he can be correct."" (Daif)"
"1337","""Whoever seeks to be a judge, and asks others to intercede for him with it, then he will be left on his own. And whoever is coerced into it, Allah sends an angel down to him so that he can be correct."" (Daif)"
"1338","Abdullah bin 'Amr narrated:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the one who bribes and the one who takes a bribe"
"1339","""When the judge passes a judgement in which he strived and was correct, then he receives two rewards. And when he judges and is mistaken, then he receives one reward."""
"1340","""How will you judge?"" He said: ""I will judge according to what is in Allah's Book."" He said: ""If it is not in Allah's Book ?"" He said: ""Then with the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)."" He said: ""If it is not in the Sunnah of Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?"" He said: ""I will give in my view."" He said: ""All praise is due to Allah, the One Who made the messenger of the Messenger of Allah suitable."""
"1341","Alqamah bin Wa'il [bin Hujr] narrated from his father who said:""A man from Hadramawt and a man from Kindah came to the Prophet (ﷺ). The Hadrami said: 'O Messenger of Allah! This person took some land of mine.' The Kindi said:'It is my land"
"1342","# Hadith Translation

**Narrated to us 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir al-Kūfī** — **Muhammad ibn Fuḍayl** narrated to us, from **Fuḍayl ibn Marzūq**, from **'Aṭiyyah**, from **Abū Sa'īd** (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:

> The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: *""Indeed, the most beloved of people to Allah on the Day of Resurrection, and the nearest to Him in station, is a just imām (leader); and the most hated of people to Allah, and the farthest from Him in station, is a tyrannical imām (leader).""*

**He (the narrator) further said:** There are narrations on this authority from 'Abdullah ibn Abī Awfā (may Allah be pleased with him).

**Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** The hadith of Abū Sa'īd is a *gharīb* (uncommon/singular) hadith — we do not know it except through this chain of narration. He graded it as *ḥasan* (good)."
"1343","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged that the oath is due from the one the claim is made against"
"1344","Abu Hurairah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed judgement based on an oath along with one witness."" Rabi'ah (one of the narrators) said: ""A son of Ibn Sa'd bin 'Ubadah informed me saying: 'We found in a book of Sa'd that the Prophet (ﷺ) passed judgement based on an oath along with a witness"
"1345","""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'No Imam closes his door on one in need, dire straits and poverty, except that Allah closes the gates of the Heavens from his dire straits, his needs, and his poverty.' So Mu'awiyah appointed a man to look after the needs of the people."""
"1346","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrated from his father:""The Prophet (ﷺ) passed judgement based on an oath along with one witness."" He said: ""And 'Ali judged between you based on it"
"1347","""My father wrote to 'Ubaidullah bin Abi Bakrah who was a judge: ""Do not pass a judgement between two people while you are angry, for indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'The judge should not judge between two people while he is angry.'"""
"1348","""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched me to Yemen. When I had left, he sent a message after me, so I returned and he said: 'Do you know why I sent a message to you ? Do not take anything without my permission, for that will be Ghulul, and whoever commits Ghulul, he comes with what he took on the Day of Judgement. This is why I called you, so now go and do your job.'"""
"1349","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Whoever frees a portion"" or he said: ""a part of a slave"
"1350","Samurah narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""The lifelong gift is permitted for its inhabitant"" or:""is an inheritance for its inhabitant"
"1351","Jabir narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""Whichever man is given a lifelong gift for himself and his offspring"
"1352","""Indeed you come to me with your disputes, and I am only a human being, perhaps one of you is more eloquent at presenting his argument than the other. If I judge for one of you, giving him something from the rights of his brother, then it is only a piece of the Fire that I am giving him, so do not take anything from it."""
"1353","# Hadith Translation

**Qutaybah narrated to us:** Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr, from his father, who said:

A man from Ḥaḍramawt and a man from Kindah came to the Prophet ﷺ. The Ḥaḍramī said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, this man has seized a piece of land that belongs to me."" The Kindī said, ""It is my land, and it is in my possession. He has no right to it.""

The Prophet ﷺ said to the Ḥaḍramī, **""Do you have proof (bayyinah)?""** He said, ""No."" He ﷺ said, **""Then you have his oath (yamīn).""** He said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the man is a wicked person (fājir); he does not care about what he swears upon, and he does not refrain from anything."" He ﷺ said, **""You have nothing from him except that.""**

The man then set out to take the oath. When he turned to leave, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, **""If he swears upon your property in order to consume it unjustly, he will surely meet Allah while He is turning away from him.""**

He (the narrator) said: In this chapter, there are narrations from ʿUmar, Ibn ʿAbbās, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, and al-Ashʿath ibn Qays.

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: The ḥadīth of Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth."
"1354","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Ali ibn Hujr, who reported from Ali ibn Mushir and others, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah, from Amr ibn Shu'aib, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet ﷺ said in his sermon:**

**""The burden of proof lies upon the claimant, and the oath is incumbent upon the one against whom the claim is made.""**

---

**Scholarly Note on the Chain of Narration (Isnad):**

This hadith has some discussion regarding its chain of narration. Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Arzami is considered weak in hadith narration on account of his memory. He was declared weak (du'if) by Ibn al-Mubarak and others.

---

## Explanation of Key Terms

- **Al-Bayyinah (البَيِّنَةُ):** The clear evidence or proof — referring to the obligation upon the claimant to produce evidence substantiating his claim.
- **Al-Mudda'i (المُدَّعِي):** The claimant or plaintiff who asserts a right or claim.
- **Al-Yamīn (اليَمِينُ):** The oath — referring to the requirement that the defendant swear an oath denying the claim if no evidence is produced by the claimant.
- **Al-Mudda'a Alayhi (المُدَّعَى"
"1355","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The oath is based upon what will make your companion believe you.” [Qutaibah (one of the narrators) said: “ What will make you believed by your companion”"
"1356","""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed judgement based on an oath along with one witness."" Rabi'ah (one of the narrators) said: ""A son of Ibn Sa'd bin 'Ubadah informed me saying: 'We found in a book of Sa'd that the Prophet (ﷺ) passed judgement based on an oath along with a witness.'"""
"1357","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""When you disagree over the road"
"1358","Abu Maimunah narrated from Abu Hurairah who said:""The Prophet (ﷺ) gave a boy the choice between his father and his mother"
"1359","""Whoever frees a portion"" or, he said: ""a part"" or he said: ""a share he owns of a slave, then he can afford the remainder of the price according to the reasonable price, then he will be free. Otherwise he has freed as much as he has freed (only)."" Ayyub (one of the narrators) said: ""Perhaps Nafi said in this Hadith: 'Meaning he has freed as much of him as he has freed.'"""
"1360","Anas narrated:""One of the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) gave the Prophet (ﷺ) some food in a bowl. Then 'Aishah broke the bowl with her hand"
"1361","Ali bin Khashram narrated to us, Isa bin Yunus informed us, from Sa'eed bin Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from An-Nadr bin Anas, from Bashir bin Nahik, from Abu Hurairah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever frees a share - or he said a portion - of a slave, then his emancipation is to be paid for from his wealth if he has wealth. But if he does not have wealth, then he is to be valued a fair valuation, then he is made to work off (the remaining value) for the portion of the one who did not free (his share), without being overburdened.'""

[Abu Eisa] said: There is also a narration on this topic from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr.

Muhammad bin Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya bin Sa'eed narrated to us, from Sa'eed bin Abi Arubah, similarly, and he said: ""Shaqisan"" (a portion).

Abu Eisa said: This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. And likewise, Aban bin Yazid narrated it from Qatadah, similar to the narration of Sa'eed bin Abi Arubah. Shu'bah also narrated this Hadith from Qatadah, but he did not mention in it the matter of working off (the debt).

The people of knowledge differed regarding the working off (the debt). Some of the people of knowledge held the view of allowing the working off (the debt) in this case, and this is the view of Sufyan Ath-Thawri and the people of Kufah, and Ishaq holds this view as well.

Some of the people of knowledge said: If a slave is owned jointly by two men, and one of them frees his share, then if he has wealth, he is liable for the share of his partner, and the slave is freed by means of his wealth. But if he does not have wealth, then only what has been freed of the slave is freed, and he is not made to work off (the remainder). They said this based on what has been reported from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (ﷺ). This is the view of the people of Madinah, and Malik bin Anas, Ash-Shafi'i, and Ahmad hold this view."
"1362","Narrated Nafi':that Ibn 'Umar said: ""I was reviewed before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the army"
"1363","Narrated Al-Bara':""My maternal uncle Abu Burdah Ibn Niyar passed by me and he had a flag with him. I said: 'Where are you going ?' He said: 'the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched me to a man who married a woman his father had married to: that I should bring him his head"
"1364","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:""A man from the Ansar disputed with Az-Zubair before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the canals of Harrah which they used to irrigate the date palms. The Ansari said: 'Let the water pass'. But he refused"
"1365","""Reconciliation is allowed among the Muslims, except for reconciliation that makes the lawful unlawful, or the unlawful lawful. And the Muslims will be held to their conditions, except the conditions that make the lawful unlawful, or the unlawful lawful."""
"1366","Sa‘īd ibn ‘Abd al-Raḥmān al-Makhzūmī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ‘Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from al-A‘raj, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: I heard him say: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When one of you seeks permission from his neighbour to fix a wooden beam in his wall, he should not refuse him.” When Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrated this, they bowed their heads. He said: “What is the matter with you? Why do you turn away from it? By Allāh, I will surely cast it between your shoulders.” He said: In this chapter, there are narrations from Ibn ‘Abbās and Mujammi‘ ibn Jāriyah. Abū ‘Īsā said: The hadith of Abū Hurayrah is a hasan sahīh hadith. This is acted upon according to some of the scholars, and this is the view of al-Shāfi‘ī. It has been narrated from some of the scholars, including Mālik ibn Anas, that he said: He may prevent his neighbour from placing his beam in his wall. The first opinion is more correct."
"1367","“The oath is based upon what will make your companion believe you.”
"
"1368","Narrated Rafi' bin Khadij:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever farms a people's land without their permission"
"1369","Narrated An-Nu'man bin Bashir:That his father gave a slave to a son of his. So he went to the Prophet (ﷺ) to have him witness it. He (ﷺ) said: 'Have you given a gift similar to this one to all of your sons?' He replied: 'No'. So he said: 'Then take him back"
"1370","Narrated Samurah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The neighbor of a home has more right to the home"
"1371","Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The neighbor has more right to his preemption. He is to be waited for even if he is absent"
"1372","""One of the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) gave the Prophet (ﷺ) some food in a bowl. Then 'Aishah broke the bowl with her hand, and discarded what was in it. So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Food for food and vessel for vessel."""
"1373","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) borrowed a bowl which broke, so he guaranteed (compensated) it for them."
"1374","that Ibn 'Umar said: ""I was reviewed before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the army, and I was fourteen years old, but he did not accept me. Then I was reviewed before him in the army later while I was fifteen years old, and he accepted me."" Nafi' said: ""I narrated this Hadith to 'Uman bin 'Abdul Azeez and he said: 'This is the limit that distinguishes between childhood and adulthood.' Then he wrote to give salaries to whoever reached fifteen years old."" 
(Another chain) from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (ﷺ) and it is similar, but he did not mention in it that 'Umar bin 'Abdul-'Aziz wrote that this is the limit that distinguishes between youth and childhood and adulthood. In his narration, Ibn 'Uyainah said (that Nafi' said): ""I narrated it to 'Umar bin 'Abdul-'Aziz and he said: 'This is the limit that distinguishes between children and soldiers.'"""
"1375","""My maternal uncle Abu Burdah Ibn Niyar passed  by me and he had a flag with him. I said: 'Where are you going ?' He said: 'the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched me to a man who married a woman his father had married to: that I should bring him his head."""
"1376","""A man from the Ansar disputed with Az-Zubair before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the canals of Harrah which they used to irrigate the date palms. The Ansari said: 'Let the water pass'. But he refused, So they brought their dispute to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Az-Zubair: 'O Zubair! Irrigate (your land) then let the water pass to you neighbor.' The Ansari became angry and said:' Is this because he is your aunt's son?' The face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) changed color. Then he said: 'O Zubair! Irrigate (your land) and then withhold the water until it reaches the walls.' Az-Zubair said: 'By Allah! I think that this Ayah was revealed about that: But no, by your Lord, they can have no Faith until they make you (O Muhammad) judge in all disputes between them, and find in themselves no resistance against your decisions and accept (them) with full submission.'"""
"1377","# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah narrated to us:** Hammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Abū al-Muhallab, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه that a man from the Anṣār freed six slaves of his at the time of his death, and he had no other wealth besides them. This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he spoke to him in severe terms. Then he called for the slaves, divided them into lots, and cast lots among them. He freed two and retained four.

It has been narrated through other chains from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه.

He (al-Tirmidhī) said: In this chapter there is also (a narration) from Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه.

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: The ḥadīth of ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* ḥadīth.

The practice according to this is held by some of the people of knowledge from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others. It is the position of Mālik, al-Shāfiʿī, Aḥmad, and Isḥāq, who held the view of employing the casting of lots (*al-qurʿah*) in this matter and in other matters.

As for some of the people of knowledge from the people of Kūfah and others, they did not approve of the casting of lots and said: one-third of each slave should be freed, and the slave should be required to work to earn the remaining two-thirds of his value.

Abū al-Muhallab's name is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr al-Jarmī, and he is not Abū Qilābah. He is also called Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr. Abū Qilābah al-Jarmī's name is ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd."
"1378","Narrated Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever possesses a mahram relative, then that relative is free."" Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: ""We do not know this hadith as musnad except through the narration of Hammad ibn Salamah. And some of them narrated this hadith from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Umar something similar to this."""
"1379","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The injuries caused by the animal are without liability"
"1380","that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever farms a people's land without their permission, then nothing he farms belongs to him and its finances are due to him."""
"1381","That his father gave a slave to a son of his. So he went to the Prophet (ﷺ) to have him witness it. He (ﷺ) said: 'Have you given a gift similar to this one to all of your sons?' He replied: 'No'. So he said: 'Then take him back.'"""
"1382","Narrated Shumair:that Abyad bin Hammal visited the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who asked him to set aside a reserve of salt(a mine). So he reserved it for him. As he was turning away"
"1383","Narrated 'Alqamah bin Wa'il:from his father that the Prophet (ﷺ) set aside a land reserve for him in Hadramawt. (One of the narrators added): ""And he sent Mu'awiyah with him to reserve it for him"
"1384","that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When the boundaries are defined and the streets are fixed, then there is no preemption."""
"1385","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:""The Prophet (ﷺ) made a deal with the people of Khaibar for half of what was produced from it"
